A static class can't receive constructor injection. You have two options:

## Option 1: Convert to a non-static class (recommended)

```csharp
public class TimestampFormatter(TimeProvider timeProvider)
{
    public string Format()
        => timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("O");
}
```

Register in DI:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System);
builder.Services.AddSingleton<TimestampFormatter>();
```

## Option 2: Keep it static, pass `TimeProvider` as a parameter

```csharp
public static class TimestampFormatter
{
    public static string Format(TimeProvider timeProvider)
        => timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("O");
}
```

Callers resolve `TimeProvider` from DI and pass it in.

---

**Option 1** is preferred — it's idiomatic DI, keeps call sites clean, and makes testing straightforward:

```csharp
// In tests (requires Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing NuGet)
var fake = new FakeTimeProvider(new DateTimeOffset(2026, 7, 8, 20, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
var formatter = new TimestampFormatter(fake);
Assert.Equal("2026-07-08T20:00:00.0000000+00:00", formatter.Format());
```

